Host serial and parallel ports: TCP, host serial devices, a parallel capture file

retrodep/parser.c is WinUAE's win32 parser.c with every host call under #if 0 (CreateFile,
GetAddrInfoW, WriteFile, ...) and select/accept/send/recv defined to 0, so no serial port
could open and nothing reached a printer. The UART emulation itself (serial_host.c) is fine
and calls openser/writeser/readser/setbaud; only the host end was missing.

- retrodep/adm_hostio.c (new) implements those functions portably: Winsock or BSD sockets,
  Win32 comm or termios. serial: "TCP://host:port" listens for one client (WinUAE's syntax),
  "TCP://host:port/connect" connects out and keeps reconnecting, anything else opens a host
  serial device. parallel: every byte strobed out is appended to a file. It includes no UAE
  header, because parser.h typedefs SOCKET and the Win32 comm structures for other platforms.
- parser.c: the stubbed printer and serial functions go under #if 0; two accessors give
  adm_hostio.c the CTS/RTS and stop-bit prefs.
- libretro-glue.c: serial_port= and parallel_port= in a .uae.
- libretro-core.c: adm_serial_service() applies the host's port request on the emulation
  thread at the top of retro_run, and re-opens it after a reload rebuilt prefs without it.
- Exports adm_serial_set_port, adm_parallel_set_output and adm_hostio_get_status.

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

